At jbonunsla 2006 I attempted to rewrite a scentance, which was itself the
product of a lengthy and uneventful school day.
This scentance was meant to take the statement: "...you can nest sumtiinside
sumti inside sumti, up to and including the point where you fry your brain."
(from the "lojban for beginners" lessons) as more of a challenge.
I had said to (atleast one person) that I would send it to them, and I wish
for as many comments on the grammar as possable, so I post my rediculously
lengthy (and historically inacurate) statement for the general evaluation of
the lojbanic community:

.i ko'a goi le catra be la cekspir. poi ke'a finti la romios.end.djuliet.
leka ce'u zdile kei le xelso lisri ku'o cu badri lenu catra la cekspir. loi
vanju kei mu'i lenu ko'a co'a facki ledu'u ko'a nelci le se ciska be la
cekspir kei la cekspir. (zo'o)


I recognise the absurdity of the statement, but it was the longest thing I
could think of off the top of my head in school, and this particular
statement was the best I could remember of it (and have edited by many
people at jbonunsla-- ki'e .iosai) at jbonunsla.
Input, comments, and corrections are more than welcome

